{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions","id":425015,"title":"Running a Demon Game for the 1st Time; Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-02T05:20:47-08:00","id":425015,"title":"Running a Demon Game for the 1st Time; Questions","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I've got players who have expressed interest in Demon (subtly but continually for the last few months) and I am looking at it again with an eye toward running it. However I have some questions about how to get things started and going. Can you help?<br /> <br /> 1. How does a Ring of Demons form? The are described as very paranoid right from the off - how do four random Demons all fall within similar time frames of each other, all within a similar geographical location and all come into contact with one another?<br /> <br /> The paranoia and mistrust, especially for someone early in their descent, seems to make forming a Ring quite...unlikely?<br /> <br /> Edit: Note, I don't want their Falls and the like to be secretly the plans and plotting of the God-Machine, I want it to be their choice, their Falls and their Descents, not to pull the rug from under them a dozen sessions in with some 'and it was the bad guy's plan all along mwahahaha!' twist thing as I know that would piss me off as a player <i>hugely</i> so why would I do it to them?<br /> <br /> 2. Ciphers. Does anyone have examples of these? I'm having a hard time coming up with ideas for them, the Interlock powers you might create from combining them and the idea that i as GM am deciding important personal character 'identity' level stuff for my players while keeping them in the dark about key parts of their characters.<br /> <br /> 3. Avoiding 'Plot of the Week'. The game seems set up wonderfully to allow for God Machine Infrastructure of the week to pop up, players tear it down, deal with fallout, rinse and repeat. There's 'making Hell' as an 'end goal' but that's fairly ambiguous and open to individual character's interpretations of it. What have <i>your</i> games had as long term goals?<br /> <br /> 4. Any general hints and tips, from hard won experience? Power combinations to watch out for, quirks in the rules, kinds of threats and challenges that are good or bad? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 03-02-2015, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T05:58:49-08:00","id":425069,"title":"","content":"<b>How does a ring form?</b><br /> <i>Vulnerability.</i> The same forces that give the Unchained a reason to be paranoid also give them a need for support, comrades in arms, and buddies to watch their backs. You can't be in every place at once, so an extra pair of eyes to keep in touch with is itself a great boon for keeping yourself safe.<br /> <i>Empathy.</i> Demons feel as vibrantly as anyone \u2014 perhaps moreso, if just for having their relatively dulled lives as angels to contrast with. The Fall can be a traumatic experience, and it's easy to imagine how the Unchained could have a need for a less logistical, more emotional kind of support. People who know the unique challenges they're put through. People who've been there and know their highs and their lows. Friends and peers.<br /> <i>Expedience.</i> Some Unchained keep their friends close and their enemies closer. If you don't know whether you can trust your fellow demons, scout them out; do a few jobs with them, get mutual goals accomplished, and in the process, find out what they're really after, whether they pose a threat, and how to insulate yourself from that threat if so.<br /> <i>Mystery.</i> Maybe there is something greater driving multiple Falls in the same location in a short period of time. The demonic mindset usually doesn't dismiss that possibility. How to find out what caused it, and why \u2014 and whether it will be a problem further down the line? Are you being used right from the start?<br /> <br /> The characters created using the chargen rules don't necessarily all have to represent demons fresh off their Fall. Demons before the start of the adventure could have been hiding out and establishing themselves for however long is plausible. The game itself is when the interesting stuff starts happening, and when demons start getting into the kind of trouble that catalyzes fast learning. And with demons' ability to disappear into the crowd, it's not hard to imagine two demons in the same city who go years without realizing the other is around, until one of them makes occult waves that prompt the other to investigate, or a local operation draws the interest of both.<br /> <br /> Once a ring has come together, through whatever means, the simple act of working together for common goals, however immediate in scope, should be able to gradually build a sense of camaraderie and deeper bonds. A ring that comes together out of mutual distrust and aloof pragmatism doesn't need to remain so forever.<br /> <br /> <b>General tips and tricks?</b><br /> The spirit rules make for beefy antagonists; even low-Rank angels are nothing for a PC to sneeze at.<br /> Compromise Conditions are harsh. Don't be nitpicky with the risk of compromise; it's not thwacking the character with a newspaper, it's hitting them with a claw hammer. The feeling of the possibility of compromise, in my experience, is more threatening and oppressive than the actual immediate danger of risking them.<br /> Not every threat, not even every physical threat, has to be on the level of an angel or other dread monster. Demons are simultaneously very effective but relatively fragile when not in their element. A simple firefight with a couple mortal humans can be plenty tense, especially given compromise can often seem an even more threatening alternative to dealing with bullets.<br /> That said, know your players' capabilities; the embeds and exploits possessed by a demon can have a big impact on the situations where they come into play. Tough guys with SMGs aren't going to figure out how to get around Check Backdrop for a good while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:41:55-08:00","id":425251,"title":"","content":"Stupid Loserman has got question 1 covered marvelously. <br /> <br /> Question 2: The Storyteller's Guide will be of use here, but it's not published yet. Here are some threads that might help.<br /> Making a Cipher. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/339493-help-how-to-make-a-cipher\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-make-a-cipher</a><br /> Making Interlocks. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/364056-associate-integrate-identity-theft-interlock-idea-help\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lock-idea-help</a><br /> <br /> Some quick and dirty tips: Ciphers can be built forwards (working towards final secret) or backwards from the final secret. Does your game have an endgame or direction mapped out? Backwards might be of use. If not, forwards is probably better. If you're really struggling, consider letting your players help. Ever played Wrath: The Oblivion? You could get players to design one of their ring-mate's Ciphers (with your help).<br /> <br /> Question 3: Come up with a big plan for the G-M. It might be a local plan or even a world-shattering one. Consider having a personal answer to the mystery of Its aims and motives. Is it preparing earth for an alien colonisation? Is it shepherding humanity's evolution? Is it entirely insane and just needs to be stopped? All of these could lead to very different overarching plans. Once you have your big plan, be it local, national or global, have your little vignettes and plots of the week hint at and link to it.<br /> <br /> Also consider building a local demonic society - build a sandbox for players to enjoy and they might take a lot of the pressure off for weekly games. They might want to join a local Agency, get revenge on that Tempter who cheated them, help out the demon who needs a Cover who did them a favor when they needed it. <br /> <br /> Question 4: Download and Fungible Knowledge are a hilarious and powerful combo to keep an eye out for. The Look is a bit nasty, though it's no use on demons or angels. Living Recorder can turn human NPCs into nightmares for the unprepared ST. None of these are game-ruining, of course, they just need to handled carefully. Really, this can be said of most Exploits and Embeds. Watch out of the demonic form ability that lets them drain Essence/Aether, too. Again, it doesn't break games, it just needs to be remembered. <br /> <br /> Stupid Loserman hits nicely on one of demon's challenges. Your PCs can use Exploits and form abilities to deal with just about any situation, but they need to be careful when doing so... In general, expect demons to expertly confound, outmaneuver and outfight humans. This is fine. Angels and other demons are another kettle of fish. Cryptids are underused, but I'm a huge fan of them, and they can run the gambit from fun challenge to nightmarish biomechanical dragon. Ghosts are a fun change of pace. Demons just don't expect 'em. <br /> <br /> Hunter angels are very powerful. I generally encourage a 'run' response, with 'learn their banes and bans' as a longer running plot. Don't forget not all angels are combatants, of course. Alexandra Fairbanks and Dizang from the core are good examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:09:00-08:00","id":425524,"title":"","content":"For Ciphers, check out the Demon Ready-Made Characters PDF. There are four complete Ciphers in that, and it's not hard to reverse engineer the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:41:31-08:00","id":425545,"title":"","content":"3. Three things spring to mind:<ul><li>Grow a living world for your players to have stories in, with people, groups and situations that change and shift. Yes, Demons fight the G-M, but they have lives that they <i>need</i> to live. Force them to juggle other obligations. They can do a stake-out tonight, but their son needs to be picked up from school.</li> <li>Emphasize that Infrastructure isn't something that can be destroyed after work before hitting the bars. It takes time, careful planning, and involves heavy amount of risk. Destroying or subverting infrastructure is something that the players works up to, raising the stakes over the course of a few sessions. In video game terms, make Infrastructure the level boss, not a random encounter.</li> <li>Give the players moral choices to wrestle with, make them aware their choices have effects on other people. Person of Interest episode &quot;Honor Among Thieves&quot; has the characters sabotage a charity that was set to help thousands of underprivileged children in order to prevent an amoral Artificial Intelligence from gaining a stranglehold on the education system.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> 4. Watch out for over-planning from your players. Bank Heist adventures where the players are endlessly working out plans and infiltration are fun the first time. If every session turns into Ocean's 11, you'll need to find ways to break it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:24:56-08:00","id":425724,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, I'll have a look for the ready-made characters.<br /> <br /> The tip on breaking up the planning I'll take to heart.<br /> <br /> I'm considering setting the game somewhere like Libya post-revolution or perhaps Israel due to the underlying hostilities so that the environment itself is more proactively hostile.<br /> <br /> I also really like the idea of the GM being broken itself...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:50:09-08:00","id":426012,"title":"","content":"Also remember that Angels don't <i>have </i>to be Antagonists all the time. Angels work to their purpose and if that purpose doesn't include the Unchained in any way they are unpredictable in their reaction to an encounter with a Demon. They may prove to be interesting foils or allies to greater plots. Not <i>everything</i> has to be the God-Machine (though I encourage the God-Machine to be your primary antagonist, as it's rather the point of the game) and so it can be interesting to have some dangerous events bring Demons and Angels together briefly as allies. If you have God-Machine Chronicle a good example is the angel Kalka. Having an Angel realise it cannot complete its task by itself means the creature will adapt, seek another way to complete that task and that method might be seeking help from its former brethren. This is a great way to present alternative antagonists like powerful Cryptids and is also a good way to bring in the element of distrust. They cannot possibly know if the Angel's leading them into a trap or if it will report them to the God-Machine as soon as its task is done or if it'll just return to storage and never mention them.<br /> <br /> Here is an example Interlock that I made for one of my players:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Key</b> \u2013 <b>Like I Built It</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>2</b></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><sup>nd</sup></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b> Key \u2013 The Map is Not the Territory</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Interlock </b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>An Image is a Window</b> </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider is able to learn the location of something simply by seeing an image of it. By reading the intimate subroutines hidden behind the image of an object or place, she is able to discern where in creation the image represents and how to get there.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Academics</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Cost: </b>None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The interlock functions in reverse, revealing to any nearby hunter angels that there is a demon and where to find it. Roll to check for compromise and gain the Flagged condition.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The interlock fails to activate. Subsequent attempts are made with a -1.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b>She knows the directions to the broad location (such as the way to the house or park).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>She knows the directions to the location down to a more specific locale, such as a room inside a building, or a particular area of a park or field.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><i>Note: This power does not allow her to locate the exact position of a hidden object that is secured in this location only that it is somewhere in that location.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I can also share the entire Cipher, if you like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 03-02-2015, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:17:16-08:00","id":426101,"title":"","content":"I too am running a Demon game for the first time and one technique I've found useful is to read spy novels and take notes of the plot twists and bits of tradecraft for reuse. It really helps give things more of a spy flavor. <br /> <br /> What I did for the PC's Ring, was tell them they were in a Ring and let them figure out how they came to know and trust each other. That generates more interesting content than any backstory I could have thought up.<br /> <br /> I have also found it fun to create NPC Demons in the setting; it's not like Minecraft, where you can just find a nice piece of Infrastructure and either smash it or leech Aether; there might be another Demon who has been working for the last five years to understand and suborn it to their own purposes, and they're going to be pissed off if the PC Demons just show up and pull the linchpin. Of course, that NPC Demon might actually be an Integrator trying to use that Infrastructure to connect with the God Machine, or trying to blow up the whole city with it; maybe you should smash it. <br /> <br /> Exiles seem really cool too but I am leery of introducing one into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:27:45-08:00","id":426259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=426012#post426012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that Angels don't <i>have </i>to be Antagonists all the time. Angels work to their purpose and if that purpose doesn't include the Unchained in any way they are unpredictable in their reaction to an encounter with a Demon. They may prove to be interesting foils or allies to greater plots. Not <i>everything</i> has to be the God-Machine (though I encourage the God-Machine to be your primary antagonist, as it's rather the point of the game) and so it can be interesting to have some dangerous events bring Demons and Angels together briefly as allies. If you have God-Machine Chronicle a good example is the angel Kalka. Having an Angel realise it cannot complete its task by itself means the creature will adapt, seek another way to complete that task and that method might be seeking help from its former brethren. This is a great way to present alternative antagonists like powerful Cryptids and is also a good way to bring in the element of distrust. They cannot possibly know if the Angel's leading them into a trap or if it will report them to the God-Machine as soon as its task is done or if it'll just return to storage and never mention them.<br /> <br /> Here is an example Interlock that I made for one of my players:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Key</b> \u2013 <b>Like I Built It</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>2</b></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><sup>nd</sup></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b> Key \u2013 The Map is Not the Territory</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Interlock </b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>An Image is a Window</b> </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider is able to learn the location of something simply by seeing an image of it. By reading the intimate subroutines hidden behind the image of an object or place, she is able to discern where in creation the image represents and how to get there.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Academics</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Cost: </b>None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The interlock functions in reverse, revealing to any nearby hunter angels that there is a demon and where to find it. Roll to check for compromise and gain the Flagged condition.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The interlock fails to activate. Subsequent attempts are made with a -1.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b>She knows the directions to the broad location (such as the way to the house or park).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>She knows the directions to the location down to a more specific locale, such as a room inside a building, or a particular area of a park or field.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><i>Note: This power does not allow her to locate the exact position of a hidden object that is secured in this location only that it is somewhere in that location.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I can also share the entire Cipher, if you like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you could share the whole thing that would be really helpful. The character in question, what is their ultimate goal/end point/etc. that made you choose those Embeds and build an interlock in that way? I could see something like 'Like I Built It' + 'The Map Is Not The Territory' leading to something with construction blueprints or design documents and pulling objects from the plans.<br /> <br /> Talking of non-GMachine antagonists, have you found any of the other supernaturals (major or minor) to be good fits? Any that really clash badly?<br /> <br /> Mages seem a great fit thematically but I've run Mage (a lot), I love Mage (a lot) and I know that Mage's toolboxes get crazy broad, I'd be worried about Allies NPC Mages doing a lot of problem solving for the players (they've played Mage a lot, so they're almost certainly more comfortable with what a Mage can pull off than what a Demon could do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:45:06-08:00","id":426758,"title":"","content":"I might be able to provide you a sample as well, if I can find the file on my Dropbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:54:39-08:00","id":426764,"title":"","content":"Best advice for Ciphers IMO - 'cold reading'. Familiarize yourself with a wikipedia entry on it. Read a little Nostradamas. Then write something that could more or less apply to hundreds of separate interpretations, and watch which one the player naturally gravitates toward. Then you can either have them be correct or pull a twist. As an example, I had, 'Thy Questions / Unto Fundament / Are Become / Thy Answers'. Try figuring out what THAT means!<br /> <br /> The best Cyphers are vague enough so that Demons can argue about what they mean with each other and not be sure they are right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:30:09-08:00","id":426816,"title":"","content":"Here we go. My caveat is that these are slightly more complicated than an Interlock probably should be. Also, my idea of combination powers is more conceptual than literal.<br /> <br /> This is the Watcher's Cipher. Her Covers were information brokers and members of the media. This character was, interestingly enough, originally a Messenger, but when <b>Interface </b>was released, we realised she was an Analyst. In other words, even the Storyteller didn't know! The God-Machine is indeed powerful...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>The Watcher</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cipher:</b> Living Recorder (Mundane) \u2192 Fungible Knowledge (Instrumental) \u2192 Lost in the Crowd (Mundane) \u2192 Everybody Knows (Vocal)<br /> <br /> <b>Final Secret: </b>\u201cMany eyes. Many knives.\u201d Nothing occurs in a vacuum. The more people see the world as you do, the more tools there are to rework it.<br /> <br /> <b>First Key: Living Recorder</b><br /> <br /> <b>Second Key: Fungible Knowledge</b><br /> <br /> <b>First </b><b>Interlock \u2013 Hawkeye</b><br /> <br /> The Watcher can briefly rewire the mind of a human to become the perfect observer.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Academics<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The Watcher\u2019s eyesight is affected instead, and it\u2019s ruined; she takes the Blind Condition for the next day.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>The effect fails.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The Watcher touches the target and alters her perception. For a number of hours equal to the Watcher\u2019s Primum, the subject of this Interlock gains the two dot version of Trained Observer, and switches the subject\u2019s highest Skill rating to Investigation. If the subject already possesses Trained Observer at two dots, he takes the three dot version. If he has that at three dots, he takes the rote quality. If Investigation is already the subject\u2019s highest rated Skill, she takes the Watcher\u2019s Investigation as a bonus. If the Watcher uses Living Recorder, she can use her subject\u2019s modified Perception pool while reviewing the footage from that Embed.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>As above, and the subject gains the Merit one step better.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Key: Lost in the Crowd</b><br /> <b>Second Interlock \u2013 Ad Hock Op</b><br /> <br /> After using Hawkeye, the Watcher can further modify her subject to become an ideal spy, and direct him to specific targets.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Subterfuge \u2013 subject\u2019s Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The subject takes the Blind condition for a number of days equal to the Watcher's Primum.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>Nothing happens.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The Watcher instructs the subject to find or spy on something/someone. For as long as he benefits from Hawkeye, he gains the 8-again quality on Stealth rolls, and does not suffer unskilled penalties, when following the Watcher\u2019s directive. The Watcher reflexively knows the subject\u2019s Stealth rating, and for an additional Aether can bolster it with her own dots in Stealth for a Scene.<br /> <br /> Once the effect of the Interlock expires, the subject will report back to the Watcher in whatever way he sees fit. Unless the Watcher specifies otherwise, the subject will remember little of this experience\u2014especially if he\u2019s caught somewhere he shouldn\u2019t be.<br /> <br /> This Interlock <i>cannot</i> force a subject to reveal something he himself wants to keep hidden.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The subject gains the Watcher's Stealth rating as a bonus at no extra Aether cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Key: Everybody Knows</b><br /> <b>Third Interlock \u2013 Memewar</b><br /> <br /> \u201cInformation wants to be free.\u201d With this Interlock, the Watcher can crowd source any problem. Anyone can be her operative. Everyone is her operative. The Watcher thinks of a problem she needs solved, or a question she needs answered. This can relate to a specific person, but it can\u2019t really reveal their secrets\u2026at least not directly. That said, this Interlock <i>can</i> sometimes reveal motive (though not intent).<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Expression<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The meme disseminates, but it gives the wrong answer. The Watcher takes a \u20135 penalty when it comes to acting on the problem.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>The effect fails and the Aether is wasted.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>For the next day, the victim is compelled to disseminate a particular meme of the Watcher\u2019s design. This can be an image, or text, or even a melody. It does not necessarily need to be an Internet meme.<br /> <br /> Anyone who encounters the meme will disseminate it further. But, as memes do, it warps, taking on aspects and shedding context until it\u2019s unrecognizable. In a number of days equal to 10 \u2013 (the Watcher\u2019s Primum) the meme will <i>become</i> the answer the Unchained desires. This will usually be nonsensical to everyone else, having become so encumbered with in-jokes and interpolations, but to the Watcher it will be revelatory. Once she collects the answer, the meme will cease to disseminate, becoming just another bit of noise in the collective.<br /> <br /> If a more concrete system is required, the Watcher should gain a +5 on any roll made to resolve her problem, or at least a variation of the Inspired Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The answer is profound. The Watcher takes the Inspired Condition as it relates to the question.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-04-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T17:44:48-08:00","id":427164,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Ms. Spider's Cipher</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Key</b> \u2013 <b>Like I Built It</b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>2</b></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><sup>nd</sup></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b> Key \u2013 The Map is Not the Territory</b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>1</b><sup><b>st</b></sup><b> Interlock </b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>An Image is a Window</b> </span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider is able to learn the location of something simply by seeing an image of it. By reading the intimate subroutines hidden behind the image of an object or place, she is able to discern where in creation the image represents and how to get there.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Academics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Cost: </b>None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The interlock functions in reverse, revealing to any nearby hunter angels that there is a demon and where to find it. Roll to check for compromise and gain the Flagged condition.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The interlock fails to activate. Subsequent attempts are made with a -1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b>She knows the directions to the broad location (such as the way to the house or park).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>She knows the directions to the location down to a more specific locale, such as a room inside a building, or a particular area of a park or field.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><i>Note: This power does not allow her to locate the exact position of a hidden object that is secured in this location only that it is somewhere in that location.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#666666\">3</span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><sup>rd</sup></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"> Key \u2013 Alibi</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>2</b><sup><b>nd</b></sup><b> Interlock</b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The Angel is its Image</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider is able to use an image of herself to revisit places she's been before by remembering the way the universe formed around her and simply repositioning her molecules. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b> Wits + Manipulation + Primum</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Cost: </b>1 Aether per 1 dot of Primum</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Not only has Ms. Spider failed to transport herself to the location she desired and possibly compromised herself, she has managed to transport herself somewhere completely new by mistake. She instead reappears at a location of the storyteller's choice (it is encouraged to be somewhat inconvenient) and she must roll to avoid compromise (-2).<br /> <b>Failure: </b>On failure, roll to avoid compromise (-2).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b>Ms. Spider rearranges herself so that all of her molecules appear at the target location exactly as she remembers, though she certainly accommodates for changes in her being since that time. Instantly transporting yourself somewhere is dangerous however and might be noticed by the God-Machine, roll to avoid compromise.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Ms. Spider's mastery over her own design has proven absolute and she has disassembled herself and reassembled herself somewhere else with perfect efficiency. She appears where she desired, does not need to roll for compromise and may remove one negative condition or tilt related to her physical health, with storyteller permission.<br /> <i>Note: This can result in time-travel. The base Interlock above assumes that no time-travel is involved, but technically space and time are the same, so a location can also account for a time. Indeed, an image is a frozen piece of time in this abstract respect. Storyteller's should be careful when allowing players to time-travel brazenly. Add additional penalties and consequences for using the interlock to time-travel.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>4</b><sup><b>th</b></sup><b> Key \u2013 Bystander Effect:</b> </span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>3</b><sup><b>rd</b></sup><b> Interlock</b></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>Magic Mirror</b> </span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider's mastery of reality and its building blocks have resulted in a dimensional understanding most demons would kill for. It may well be that this understanding will prove instrumental in the creation of a very real and physical hell one day.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b> Wits + Manipulation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Cost: </b>5 Aether per (Primum x 10 yards)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dramatic Failure: </b>Ms. Spider's attempt to create her own pocket of the world has completely backfired. Not only has she failed to create it but The God-Machine has sensed the interference in its designs and has sent angels to reacquire her immediately. Ms. Spider gains the Hunted Condition (Persistent) and the storyteller should immediately create the appropriate amount of angels that appear nearby to begin looking. <br /> <b>Failure: </b>Ms. Spider fails to create the splinter and must roll to avoid compromise (-2).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b>Ms. Spider has successfully created a splinter that is identical to the area immediately around her. The splinter is populated by any human beings that lived within the area of effect at the time of the interlock's use. It does not however create such copies of supernatural creatures, such as vampires, werewolves, mages and so on. The splinter is free from the influence of the God-Machine. It is automatically connected to any portal in the original location of the demon's choice but once this choice is made, it is permanent. The demon can choose to destroy their splinter at any time but doing so kills any beings inside. The splinter acts as a suborned infrastructure but cannot store more Aether than was expended to create it. The demon can only maintain her Primum in splinters at any given time. <i>Example: A demon with Primum 3 may only have 3 unique splinters created this way in their ownership at any given time.</i><br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Ms. Spider has so artfully created her new domain that she may at any time choose to spend a point of Aether to turn any door into the entrance of the splinter. Only one door may lead to the splinter at any time and the change only lasts 1 scene or 1 hour, whichever comes first. Whenever someone leaves the splinter it is always from the door they entered through. This effect only applies to that splinter and no other splinter in her possession may take advantage of this (unless they too were created with an exceptional success.)<br /> <i>Note: The splinter began when Ms. Spider successfully cast the Interlock, the splinter resets at midnight Primum days (plus 1 day per Aether used) after this. Individuals that reliably enter the area will have copies that reliably enter the area every day. Generic human copies, such as crowds and people who travel the street will also appear. These individuals will neither realise they are copies, or that they are in a splinter, nor is it entirely clear where they go when they cross the edge of the splinter. Crossing the edge of the splinter for any character from outside the splinter, including Ms. Spider, causes them to appear on the opposite side of the splinter.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Final Secret: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The promised land is built, not conquered.</span></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Ms. Spider fell for but the grace of Man. Her sympathies led her astray from the God-Machine's design for her \u2013 to create angelic beings known as Dalga, to be a mother to mothers uncounted. She denied this design because she saw a flaw in her creation; the Dalga had to injure and kill creatures in order to reproduce. This form of creation was flawed, it was little more than re-purposing hardware. Now she strives to find a true form of creative power, so that one day she may be a God-Machine unto herself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Ms. Spider was a Psychopomp who was tired of building and not <i>creating</i>. She fell when she destroyed the Dalga she had nurtured and created for the God-Machine because it had in turn killed and re-purposed one of the students of Seattle University. All the members of my game's ring were part of the same Infrastructure, a facility hidden in the Seattle University complex, that's purpose was to study an object and the captured Demon whom had discovered it. Ms. Spider was the builder of the facility, she folded the places between space, she built the servitors that cleaned the halls, she built the cryptids that ate the aether (something she had to deal with later, those pesky Gremlins) and hid the facility from Demonic attention. However, a series of accidents, caused four of the angels in the facility to fall. (This subsequently ensured that a powerful destroyer was activated as per the God-Machine's contingency.) They banded together out of mutual need; they were all tagged for destruction by the same powerful hunter angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T23:50:04-08:00","id":427489,"title":"","content":"Thanks you two, those help a lot. I'll have to try my hand at it once I get some stuff from my players.<br /> <br /> How do people handle Demon 'society' in a place? As in, the 4 PCs are a Ring and there are some number (I'm thinking 15-20) other Demons in the same geographical area. How have you organised it? How do they communicate between different groups? DO they communicate? How would a Temporal Agency try to attract other Demons to it to buy Covers? How would different Agendas make contact and draw people in?<br /> <br /> If these Demons are all trying to hide themselves and are all so expert at doing so how does anyone even begin finding other Demons to start forming an Agency or working with likeminded Agendas at all?<br /> <br /> Also, how do Demons find out that the GMachine is up to something with Infrastructure. Is it just through noticing strange things in the newspaper, or word of mouth or odd planning permission notices? Or is the aetheric resonance attracting them? Or are they just wandering around and just see the gears somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 03-04-2015, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T00:12:10-08:00","id":427497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=427489#post427489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these Demons are all trying to hide themselves and are all so expert at doing so how does anyone even begin finding other Demons to start forming an Agency or working with likeminded Agendas at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fa\u00e7ades, burner Covers, and Mundane Embeds all go a very very long way toward facilitating &quot;trust-building&quot; meetings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T01:25:49-08:00","id":427524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=427497#post427497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fa\u00e7ades, burner Covers, and Mundane Embeds all go a very very long way toward facilitating &quot;trust-building&quot; meetings.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that seems to assume that the Demon already knows that there are other Demon's out there to contact and has arranged a method of communication wit one or more of them already.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a Demon. You know other Demons exist in this city. You have discovered a GMachine plot and want to ruin it. You need help. How do you contact other Demons to get their help, bearing in mind you currently have no contacts with them yet?<br /> <br /> Or, you're newly fallen, you've made your way into a city and have managed to get a handle on these new, crazy feelings of this new, vital world around you. You know that <i>you've</i> broken free of the GMachine, but unless your task as an Angel required knowledge of Demons you may very well not know other Demons exist at all (why would the GM tell you about Demons if you are not meant to have any contact with them in your task? It would be unnecessary information), how would you become exposed to Demon 'society' in the first place?<br /> <br /> I might bypass this stage by having one or more players already connected to 'society'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T01:29:28-08:00","id":427525,"title":"","content":"Established Demons usually find the newly Fallen Unchained as they fall. A fall is a tumultuous event that creates a massive aetheric resonance. While it can appear subtle (though most of the time explosive) to the naked eye it reverberates on a massive scale. It isn't simply hunter angels that appear to locate the new Demon but also other Demons. As Satchel said Facades, burner Covers and Mundane Embeds all go a long way in protecting the &quot;Recruiter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Furthermore an &quot;Elysium&quot; might be set up, at your discretion as storyteller, to act as a safe and secure location for Demons to be Demons. One such location is in Splintered City: Seattle in the form of &quot;Hell on Earth&quot;, a dingy bar with a bolt-hole re-purposed into a Demon's-Only Lounge. How easily and how often Demons communicate with each other is entirely up to the mood of your chronicle and the themes you're hoping to put forward. Do you want your chronicle to be especially paranoid? Do you want betrayal to be around every corner? If this is the case then a safe, neutral place is unlikely to help facility that atmosphere so don't make one. Alternatively if you're hoping to focus on the more techgnostic factors of the chronicle then perhaps it will benefit from neutral ground.<br /> <br /> In the former case recruiters might be the only Demons that respond to a Fall and search, this process of searching might takes weeks or months after a Demon falls and might represent the beginning of a chronicle. That is to say: The players begin after they've finally been uncovered; not by the God-Machine but by another Demon through the simple process of investigation. This method certainly would capture the feeling of spy-novels. It also benefits for the Demons in this kind of chronicle to communicate through esoteric methods such as numbers stations, spray painting obscure symbols on the walls of key locations.<br /> <br /> In the latter case recruiters are likely to be present almost nightly at your neutral ground. Here your players might find representatives of each of the Agendas seeking to get another body among their cause mingling with the recruiters of more organised Agencies. You could enjoy playing with stories that might evoke a bit of a &quot;Speak-Easy&quot; feel with the neutral ground you've made occasionally coming under scrutiny of the God-Machine and so having to pick up and move. Easy enough, since it's a Bolt-Hole, but getting everyone out without the shit hitting the fan might make a fun event.<br /> <br /> If you've ever played Changeling the Lost then I would recommend considering that Demonic interaction is similar in concept to this. Changelings have great difficulty trusting anyone as they couldn't trust anything in Arcadia to be what it appeared to be. Similarly, Demons can't trust anything or anyone to appear what it appears to be. Their Cover's wife might be another Demon in disguise or a Sleeper waiting for a specific set of conditions to come into play before she kills him in his sleep. But both groups <i>need</i> to trust <i>someone</i> eventually or they're going to be on their own and they're going to die. For Changelings this comes in the form of the Motley and the Courts. For Demons this is the Ring and the Agendas (or the Agencies). Eventually a Demon needs the company of their own kind so they need to look for them. This search might begin on the internet, ordinary investigations into bizarre incidents, and may have them bumping heads with other supernaturals before finally finding their own kind.<br /> <br /> Communication likely happens through the use of special software allowing access to certain chat-rooms on the internet or dead-drop conference like pen-pals. Or it might happen face to face if you have a safe place to congregate. It's probably important in either respect to consider the manners of the Demons, such as the fact that unless they belong in a Ring together Demons are probably going to avoid (if possible) at least initial communication in one of their core Covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 03-04-2015, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T01:58:11-08:00","id":427535,"title":"","content":"That helps a lot.<br /> <br /> I've had one player say they are explicitly interested in a newly fallen, fish out of water, no idea what's going on character (the others have yet to mention anything about characters) and I was really wondering just HOW that character fits in or, even worse, if everyone goes for newly fallen.<br /> <br /> I'll try pitching that at least one of the others PCs is more connected and hand out maybe a few bonus dots (1-3) for social contacts so they can be slightly more 'established' as an in for the rest of the group, but that'll depend on what else people are planning on playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T04:46:06-08:00","id":427611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=427489#post427489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks you two, those help a lot. I'll have to try my hand at it once I get some stuff from my players.<br /> <br /> How do people handle Demon 'society' in a place? As in, the 4 PCs are a Ring and there are some number (I'm thinking 15-20) other Demons in the same geographical area. How have you organised it? How do they communicate between different groups? DO they communicate? How would a Temporal Agency try to attract other Demons to it to buy Covers? How would different Agendas make contact and draw people in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unchained society, in my games, is very much based around niches. You know in movies spies have a network of useful contacts, most often seen when they go rogue? That's how I run things. In my current game, for example, I have a Tempter who'll get you cheap Covers if you're in a bind or want/need a burner Cover, He gets the raw materials from the homeless (most of his Covers come with nasty downsides like criminal records, addictions and mental health problems). There's a demon called the Courier who has a taxi driver and a van driver as Covers. He moves things - objects, people - for a price (but he is emphatically not a getaway driver) in his gadgetted vehicles. Another demon is a gadget-expert, who makes them, unmakes them, examines them and offers guidance making them. One is an information-broker. One offers extradimensional spaces as secure meeting places,<br /> <br /> This keeps demonic society from crumbling into a paranoid, uncommunicative mess. Dealing with other Unchained (sure, it's nearly always transactional) builds relationships. You might pass on tidbits of information (unless you're a particularly selfish Tempter or secretive Inquisitor), telling them about the new angel in town, to watch out for the Exile in the abandoned hospital, that sort of thing. And like-minded demons are eventually drawn together and Agencies begin to coalesce from rings and individuals.<br /> <br /> Agencies that are actively courting demons will, as Satchel says, offer services. Cheap Covers, safehouses (supernatural or mundane), access to Agency-funds, that sort of thing. They'll also market heavily based on their ideology. For example, an Agency that oppose the God-Machine in a sustainable and careful manner will advertise to Saboteurs (we're stronger together!) and Inquisitors (we'll share information for a brighter future).<br /> <br /> For first-time communication, there's an Embed tailor-made for this. Special Message. Demons scrawl graffiti designed for demons to spot saying 'I'm new!' or perhaps 'New guy, we're here to help. Here's an internet key to find our secure ring.' or 'Here's a number for a burner phone. Call it.' A fun way demons can recognise each other is to use their faculty with languages. In downtown New York, how often do you hear someone speaking a mix of Welsh, Urdu and Romansh? Of course, angels are just as good with languages...You might even want a demon who works as a 'greeter' for the local Unchained society. They might be a nice, relatively altruistic demon or a Tempter planning to extort the helpless newbies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how do Demons find out that the GMachine is up to something with Infrastructure. Is it just through noticing strange things in the newspaper, or word of mouth or odd planning permission notices? Or is the aetheric resonance attracting them? Or are they just wandering around and just see the gears somewhere? </div> </div> </div>All of the above! Some Infrastructure is in the plain sight, if you've got Unseen Sense: God-Machine, though it's likely to be protected or hidden in more mundane ways. (Sure, the Golden Gate Bridge is Infrastructure. What're you going to do, blow it up? No, stop that, put those explosives away...). Aetheric resonance will draw cautious attention from curious demons - is it Infrastructure, a new demon, someone building a gadget? And some demons are conspiracy theorists, which is a reasonable position in a world straddled by the God-Machine. They're the ones looking at strange things in the newspaper, putting pins in maps where people saw UFOs and smiling as the pins form the shape of a wheel. And word of mouth is a thing. While demons are paranoid as a rule and some won't share their secrets, it makes sense to lots of them to share information to allies or even just demons you've worked with (as I mentioned above). The new construction project is hiding mysterious Infrastructure? Mention it, maybe they know more, and maybe they'll tell you. New hunter angel in town? Tell them, next time they might want warn you and save your skin<br /> <br /> By the way, if you still want help with Ciphers/Interlocks, PM me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 03-08-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:08:22-08:00","id":428936,"title":"","content":"Game is organised for next Wednesday, character creation, I may get back to you with some questions about building their Ciphers.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:20:26-07:00","id":432604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=427489#post427489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks you two, those help a lot. I'll have to try my hand at it once I get some stuff from my players.<br /> <br /> How do people handle Demon 'society' in a place? As in, the 4 PCs are a Ring and there are some number (I'm thinking 15-20) other Demons in the same geographical area. How have you organised it? How do they communicate between different groups? DO they communicate? How would a Temporal Agency try to attract other Demons to it to buy Covers? How would different Agendas make contact and draw people in?<br /> <br /> If these Demons are all trying to hide themselves and are all so expert at doing so how does anyone even begin finding other Demons to start forming an Agency or working with likeminded Agendas at all?<br /> <br /> Also, how do Demons find out that the GMachine is up to something with Infrastructure. Is it just through noticing strange things in the newspaper, or word of mouth or odd planning permission notices? Or is the aetheric resonance attracting them? Or are they just wandering around and just see the gears somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the funny thing about Agencies. There are four kinds of them, each one associated with a different Agenda. Temporal reflect Tempters building their Hell. Free Agencies share information, and Paranoid demons seek info. Compromised agenda lends itself to a group of Turncoats, who tend to associate with angels anyways. And so on. <br /> <br /> The simple truth is that most demons avoid Agencies as it is. They don't trust them, since its all too easy for an angel to sneak in, or that Tempter to start using some favors to steal all your Gadgets and claimed Infrastructure. So, demon &quot;society&quot; such as it is tends to be more like werewolf packs. They each claim their own little slice of Hell On Earth, rely on it to recharge their aether and build defenses around that. They run into other demons, get contact information and the like, the more they run around dealing with plots. <br /> <br /> That's how demon society grows. Word of mouth as you meet people. You know a guy who knows a guy. Demons sense aether, so that's the main reason why they can figure out who each other are in close proximity to each other. Its a slowly growing web of hush, hush meetings.<br /> <br /> If you need help with running into more demons, I personally suggest letting everyone have Aether Sense always active for free. Demons that want to hide can spoof automatically. Those that don't want to hide stand out more. Aether sense is rather limited in range as it is, and large explosions of power are rare, shy of someone making a powerful Gadget or Going Loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:57:13-07:00","id":433657,"title":"","content":"Another question popped up. When does 'Acting Grossly Out of Character' apply for a Compromise?<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the school crossing guard sneaking into the bins out back of a large office to steal the shredded remains of documents is acting pretty damn out of character but that feels like making any attempts at sneaky espionage a Compromise because most people - amazingly enough - don't go about sneaking into places and spying on people, stalking them, unpicking the details of their lives, etc. Celebrity Tabloid journalists maybe...<br /> <br /> What kind of things do you let slip and when would you press for the Compromise roll? I'm looking for the nuance and <i>why</i> you'd press one but not the other. The obvious stuff like killing someone is already called out in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:09:19-07:00","id":433678,"title":"","content":"Oh, also Stigmatics.<br /> <br /> Coming into contact with the GMs Infrastructure, Angels, etc. makes a mortal into a Stigmatic. Does interaction with a Demon do the same? What if the mortal were subject to an Exploit or particularly egregious use of an Embed? Joining a Demon's Cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:28:16-07:00","id":433728,"title":"","content":"What triggers Stigmata is vague, not even interaction with Angels and the God-Machine <i>always</i> results in Stigmata. Usually it has to be some life-changing event that opens their eyes to greater workings of the universe. Joining a God-Machine cult, even one that names their patron correctly, wouldn't necessarily induce Stigmata. While physically encountering an extra-dimensional space in the janitor's closet full of impossible clockwork might. Generally speaking Angels and Demons don't seem to <i>cause</i> Stigmata on their own but inflict it with abilities (there is an Exploit for it, after all). However, I'd say an Angel's fall would qualify and select, particularly explosive confrontations mortals might get caught in between the God-Machine and his fallen angels.<br /> <br /> Compromise checks first should be acknowledged, or &quot;seen&quot; by someone (or something, security systems count). Spy-craft is subtle and the general rule of thumb is it only makes a compromise if it's reasonably going to cause an onlooker (either the guy in the security office or a bystander) to double-take. The overweight guy who loves his iced doughnuts deciding that it was time to lose weight and only eating salad isn't cognitively dissonant. It's unusual, but people will slap him on the back, or tease him. The overweight guy who loves his iced doughnuts drinking battery acid thanks to a glitch he's picked up, however, would be a compromise.<br /> <br /> Spy-craft should only cause a compromise, in essence, if you get caught. If the player successfully makes their stealth, subterfuge and persuasion rolls to bypass notice then the player probably shouldn't be Compromised. My rule of thumb though, your mileage may vary on what you feel is logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:53:01-07:00","id":433763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=433657#post433657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question popped up. When does 'Acting Grossly Out of Character' apply for a Compromise?<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the school crossing guard sneaking into the bins out back of a large office to steal the shredded remains of documents is acting pretty damn out of character but that feels like making any attempts at sneaky espionage a Compromise because most people - amazingly enough - don't go about sneaking into places and spying on people, stalking them, unpicking the details of their lives, etc. Celebrity Tabloid journalists maybe...<br /> <br /> What kind of things do you let slip and when would you press for the Compromise roll? I'm looking for the nuance and <i>why</i> you'd press one but not the other. The obvious stuff like killing someone is already called out in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does depend on the cover. The rule of thumb ,as I understand it, is to have a general idea on the behavior of the cover determined when the character starts using it as the basis for where compromise comes from. For example lets say your cover was a former soldier who now deplores violence to the point of pacifism .That the cover has decorations for military service and significant combat ability despite being a pacifist still fits in. This person deciding to professional boxer is gonna meet some stares because there's a large gap between &quot;I don't like seeing people get hurt,&quot; and &quot;I would like to become champion of a sport that centers around trying to beat the tar out of my fellow human beings.&quot; I'm seeing it compared to breaking points a few times in the core, so it probably would be worth cross-referencing the rules for breaking points and compromise to see if it makes any more sense.<br /> <br /> As for your Stigmatic question. Well page 168 has an exploit that lets you make someone a Stigmatic. At least one exploit has it as a potential side effect on a success, so the more flashy and egregious exploits might be grounds to do it. I would be more hesitant about it with embeds because embeds are more subtle and don't really have the same potential to shatter a persons view of reality that an exploit would. A blatant use of an embed might cause compromise I would be hesitant about them causing Stigmatics. Joining a cult might have it as a thing that happens, but I don't think just joining the cult would make one a Stigmatic. Otherwise just interacting with a demon will not cause a person to become a Stigmatic unless something happens that causes them to come in contact with the GM. Oh yeah going loud and fighting an angel will probably result in nearby mortals fleeing in terror and becoming Stigmatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:58:43-07:00","id":433764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=433728#post433728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What triggers Stigmata is vague, not even interaction with Angels and the God-Machine <i>always</i> results in Stigmata. Usually it has to be some life-changing event that opens their eyes to greater workings of the universe. Joining a God-Machine cult, even one that names their patron correctly, wouldn't necessarily induce Stigmata. While physically encountering an extra-dimensional space in the janitor's closet full of impossible clockwork might. Generally speaking Angels and Demons don't seem to <i>cause</i> Stigmata on their own but inflict it with abilities (there is an Exploit for it, after all). However, I'd say an Angel's fall would qualify and select, particularly explosive confrontations mortals might get caught in between the God-Machine and his fallen angels.<br /> <br /> Compromise checks first should be acknowledged, or &quot;seen&quot; by someone (or something, security systems count). Spy-craft is subtle and the general rule of thumb is it only makes a compromise if it's reasonably going to cause an onlooker (either the guy in the security office or a bystander) to double-take. The overweight guy who loves his iced doughnuts deciding that it was time to lose weight and only eating salad isn't cognitively dissonant. It's unusual, but people will slap him on the back, or tease him. The overweight guy who loves his iced doughnuts drinking battery acid thanks to a glitch he's picked up, however, would be a compromise.<br /> <br /> Spy-craft should only cause a compromise, in essence, if you get caught. If the player successfully makes their stealth, subterfuge and persuasion rolls to bypass notice then the player probably shouldn't be Compromised. My rule of thumb though, your mileage may vary on what you feel is logical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that seems a fully workable rule of thumb and Stigmatics then seem to be a 'when dramatically appropriate' thing rather than something the player's should be worried about leaving like a trail in their wake just for doing their 'thing'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T03:00:33-07:00","id":433765,"title":"","content":"You will want to work out with the players what constitutes &quot;acting grossly out of character&quot; and being sure you are on the same page. This can be very restrictive or only come up in extreme circumstances depending on the tone you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:19:26-07:00","id":434077,"title":"","content":"One thing I rule is that its not so much acting out of Cover, its that people catching you acting out of Cover that's a big deal. The rationale is that the God Machine is hooked up not only to every Infrastructure and Angel, but to the average person, and can see through their eyes, effectively.<br /> <br /> Think of the Matrix, near the end of the first movie. The agents are trying to chase Trinity and Morpheus. The two of them reach a phone booth. The call comes out, they answer the phone. A bum sees Trinity vanish, and then suddenly, the agents know where they are. They couldn't do a general search without using people as their eyes.<br /> <br /> EDIT - in your example, its not so much the crossing guard doing something out of character that gets them with a compromise check, its someone -finding- them doing something they shouldn't. Then the flag goes up.<br /> <br /> I know its not quite the same thing, but I find it makes things easier game wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-09-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:59:05-07:00","id":434168,"title":"","content":"The book sure is vague, isn't it? Here are the guidelines for avoiding Compromise I gave to my players. They are intended to foster paranoia and roleplaying without forcing constant Compromise rolls, which can take the whole game sideways. I also like to use MCN's idea that the God-Machine is using people as part of its search grid. My head canon is that the G-M is looking for the specific emotional signature of &quot;WTF!?! What just happened? Is that guy on drugs?&quot; in bystanders.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Live your Cover.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Big Brother Is Watching.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3) A Little Tradecraft Goes a Long Way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:32:20-07:00","id":435205,"title":"","content":"Pendragon came up with some house rules modifying demon along those lines MCN. I particularly enjoy using many of his rules. One of them is in reference to people being part of the system. Human beings that are &quot;part of the system&quot; don't get to apply resistance attributes to Demon rolls because they're essentially extras but the God-Machine uses them likewise as eyes and ears, meaning anything remotely supernatural and bam. This latter part already happens since you get a -2 to Compromise if you're witnessed by a mortal in the base game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:46:05-07:00","id":436169,"title":"","content":"I am running short on time right now so if you don't mind I'm going to quote myself from earlier conversations where applicable and keep it short with original commentary right now. Hopefully that'll help!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Your question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=427489#post427489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people handle Demon 'society' in a place? As in, the 4 PCs are a Ring and there are some number (I'm thinking 15-20) other Demons in the same geographical area. How have you organised it? How do they communicate between different groups? DO they communicate? How would a Temporal Agency try to attract other Demons to it to buy Covers? How would different Agendas make contact and draw people in?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74556-how-organized-is-demon-society?p=74645#post74645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, my take is that it's a lot like the cell structure of Hunter. You might know a couple of demons outside of your ring in a personal way but mostly Demon &quot;society&quot; works through a list of phone numbers, emails and dead drops. There might be territory or specific things claimed by specific demons, but I imagine it's mostly a matter of hearsay and it's less enforced and more handled as a gentleman's agreement not to mess with each other's stuff.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Agencies are shining beacons of &quot;society&quot;, organizations based on encouraging interaction and cooperation between the Unchained. By default in my games, this is seen as something to be wary of, groups that are seen as either naive enough to think everyone's going to get along selflessly or manipulative and ruthless enough to embroil everyone in their schemes. Those perceptions plus the fact that it's relatively easy to track down info on Agencies mean it's usually seen as entirely too open to being suborned by the God-Machine and only a resource you should use when there are no easy alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small note to tack onto this: in general what I'd probably emphasize in this environment of extremely decentralized communication is that unlike other, more political games each Ring is essentially their own greatest authority. You don't have higher-ups or societal duties by default; you might know how to contact a couple of other demons and maybe even have some associates, but your Ring's business is your own and nobody's got the right to contradict you. On the other hand, nobody's going to hold your hand and if you get in trouble there's no obligation to come to your rescue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Your question, continued</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these Demons are all trying to hide themselves and are all so expert at doing so how does anyone even begin finding other Demons to start forming an Agency or working with likeminded Agendas at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my view, Demon society in general is very much voluntary; you get out what you put into it, even if that's a name and a phone number to reach you at. I imagine Rings pick a spokesman and these spokesmen work to get connected, putting out a title, what the Ring is about, and a way to get in contact. Once trust is established, I figure the most connected Rings set up a system - check in twice a month with updates, and then maybe your fellow Demon will introduce you to his friend when you're in need.<br /> <br /> Of course, once you're -that- connected, you're only a hop, skip and jump away from forming Agencies, and everyone knows how risky THAT is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Your question, continued</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how do Demons find out that the GMachine is up to something with Infrastructure. Is it just through noticing strange things in the newspaper, or word of mouth or odd planning permission notices? Or is the aetheric resonance attracting them? Or are they just wandering around and just see the gears somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Your question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/425015-running-a-demon-game-for-the-1st-time-questions?p=433657#post433657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of things do you let slip and when would you press for the Compromise roll? I'm looking for the nuance and <i>why</i> you'd press one but not the other. The obvious stuff like killing someone is already called out in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/264940-confused-about-cover?p=266022#post266022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing to remember about compromise rolls gained by out-of-character behavior is that it\u2019s for when you act <b>grossly</b> out of character. It\u2019s not so much for when you go \u201chuh, I wouldn\u2019t have guessed that\u201d when you find out your boss knows a smattering of French, or when you go \u201cwow, I never would have expected you to do that!\u201d like if the previously fat programmer loses a significant amount of weight. It\u2019s for when your octogenarian pacifist takes down five thugs with moves that would make Jason Bourne blush, or when you find the friendly pastor with a bloody machete and a bunch of chopped up bodies. It\u2019s up to the ST and the player to come to an understanding of course, but in general the guideline I go with is that if it causes a hypothetical bystander to suffer some amount of cognitive dissonance, that\u2019s when I break out the compromise rolls. So with that perspective a stock broker poking around a construction site is weird but it doesn\u2019t make you sit up and go \u201cwait a minute, a stock broker -here-? RED FLAG!\u201d As such, demons can get away with a lot of the basic legwork for their operations before they start risking cover on doing things that they blatantly shouldn\u2019t be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T02:53:18-07:00","id":438222,"title":"","content":"Right, character creation is complete (there may be some tweaking of them before the first game session next week but they should be pretty much fixed). If people are still willing to help out with Ciphers that would be appreciated!<br /> <br /> I'd like to crowdsource one Cipher to start with then try my hand at it myself for the others and see if that works.<br /> <br /> I noticed that the most fun was had in the Demonic Forms part of character gen (only one player didn't take terrible form and two of them took terrible form at rank 4) so I'm probably going to have to make sure that I'm not <i>too</i> hardcore on Compromise for using Demonic Form - my players clearly want to be able to play around with that.<br /> <br /> Integrator as an Agenda had everyone proactively comment on their confusion as to why anyone would play it.<br /> <br /> Could you help me with making the Cipher for:<br /> <br /> A Guardian who was sent to protect an up and coming Yakuza thug and reached a point of asking <i>why</i> she should be doing this at all. Concept is strongly focused on being a researcher particularly on theology, philosophy and morality and for what reasons the GMachine does what it does. Obviously an Inquisitor. Cover is an academic at a University in the philosophy and ethics department. She is playing the most 'classically' combat capable member of the group.<br /> <br /> Cover risking specialty: swords (under weaponry)<br /> <br /> Merits: library 1, resources 1, status: university 1, terrible form 4, versatile transformation 1, interdisciplinary specialty: theology 1, professional training: academic 1, fighting finesse 2, light weapons 1 (was given 3 dots for free social merits to provide links to organisations and such in the world)<br /> <br /> Embeds/Exploits: First Strike, authorized, password entropy, <b>Voice of the machine</b> (first key)<br /> <br /> Demonic Form: A classical angelic figure, strongly reminiscent of her form as an Angel, sword, wings, fire, and glory<br /> Blade hand, fast attack, inhuman reflexes, mantle of fire, glory and terror, wings, voice of the angel (she has terrible form at 4 dots but has not yet chosen the additional form options)<br /> <br /> Cipher Guidance: When discussing this she had a hard time coming to an ultimate idea but everything was very much a case of 'the truth will out' or 'knowing the answer to why'<br /> <br /> For the Cipher I was thinking Voice of the machine &gt; Find the leak &gt; Data retrieval &gt; Like I Built it<br /> <br /> 1st interlock would mean that by listening to the GMachine you can find the most vulnerable point in the local infrastructure to find out more information about what is going on<br /> <br /> 2nd interlock something like once you find the leak you can scan the GMachine's plans and history with voice of the machine so find out what it was planning to do 3 months ago, a year ago, etc<br /> <br /> 3rd I wanted to give a bonus to scanning infrastructure to find out its weak points, what it is for, what each component in the infrastructure does and how to take advantage of it (using the system in the player's guide for investigating infrastructure)<br /> <br /> Am I going in the right direction? How would you guys go about the interlocks mechanically?<br /> <br /> The idea here is to chain going from getting a hint about goings on to finding where to go for more detail, to being able to gather lots of specific detail with the option to use that detail to take control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:08:44-07:00","id":438360,"title":"","content":"How to stop it being god machine plot of the week?<br /> Well in my game which has been going on for a few months is just one plot of the god machine. Yes there are others going around that demons can find but the main one is still on going. Half the game is trying to find out what the machine is planning. If it is a good thing for demons or not. Sometimes it will be good for some and not others and demon will fight over it.<br /> This was my plot if it helps. It is a simple plan. 1. Build infrastructure (and take old ones that was broken by demons) in the fractures and then port them into the real world. 2. Shut down the shards of reality in the process too.<br /> <br /> That was it but my players had to 1st learn of the shards and how they worked. How to get in and out.<br /> Second is an occult matrix is built from other infrastructure. Basically plans within plans. One of my demons had a drug dealer cover, and he found a new mind controlling drug on the street. It made people aggressive and unreasonable. This was to cause more gang warfare (with the help of cultist and angels rubbing up people the wrong way) - Concealment infurstrtre<br /> <br /> This was to help give momentum so an angel with a cover of a politician trying to get militated police to sort the salutation out (really they were demon hunters who could be free to take out demons in board daylight. They were there to protect the matrix and distract demons from the matrix) - defence infrastructure<br /> <br /> One of the player demons job was to collect probability and his npc wife took fate, this was needed to make the stuff from the shards become more real and be able to exist in the real world. - logistical infrastructure<br /> <br /> There are more infrastructure to make this whole plan work, some that would stop the plan out right and some that would barely slow it down. My players have be investigating this project for a while (in between personal plot and someone trying to create souls) and they are close to knowing what the plot is about. They know the purpose of the drugs and the plan to put demon hunters on the street and that weird things are happening in the shards but not sure what. They have angel jacked the politician\u2019s cover to stop that plan and are going to raid the demon hunter training ground to stop that plan (still not knowing what the god machines plan is)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The point I'm making, it should not be easy to know what the god machine is planning and it should not always be easy to just break down infrastructure. The infrastructure might not be easy to take down as it is made of people who work at a shop. The demons might have a problem killing inncent people, unaware of what they are doing. Half the battle should be knowing anything, and the way demons are they do not like to share info for free and they can always lie. The second should be who does this affect. Who would help ypu stop it and who would try and stop you (humans, demons, angel or even vampires). Then (unless they have a certain exploit) they then need to find out to take the thing down.<br /> <br /> This shouldnt feel like a plot of the week (hopefully)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}